From 68c105ce25e6280b0840b0d51b66b5dbd30d5976 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Elias=20Nyk=C3=A4nen?=
 <61413159+Eliasny@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 04:25:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plugin): allow discovery over #None with the secure-only
 server config

UA_ServerConfig_setDefaultWithSecureSecurityPolicies adds no
SecurityPolicy#None. A client therefore cannot call GetEndpoints or
FindServers to learn the endpoints and the server certificate, although
Part 4, 5.4.1 requires these services without message security. A
connection is only possible if the client already knows the server
certificate. This also breaks GDS pull and push clients, which discover
the endpoints of a server before it trusts them (Part 12).

Add SecurityPolicy#None for the discovery services only
(securityPolicyNoneDiscoveryOnly). No endpoint and no UserTokenPolicy is
created for #None, so every Session stays secured. The server_encryption
example no longer needs to add #None itself.

Fixes #6771
